---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Stream new heads or logs, or query logs over a block range

Usage: rustman evm logs [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --address <ADDRESS>
          Logs from this contract (repeatable; any contract when absent)

      --event <SIGNATURE>
          Topic 0 as an event signature: "Transfer(address,address,uint256)"

      --topic <TOPIC>
          A further topic, in order (32-byte hex, a signature, or * for any)

      --heads
          Stream new block headers instead of logs

      --from-block <BLOCK>
          Query logs from this block instead of streaming (with --to-block, default latest)

      --to-block <BLOCK>
          The last block of a query

      --max-events <N>
          Stop streaming after N events (reorged logs not counted)

      --duration <DURATION>
          Stop streaming after this long: 30s, 5m

      --poll-interval <DURATION>
          How often to poll over HTTP (default 2s)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --rpc <URL>
          The node: a URL or a {{variable}} (default: the environment's {{rpc}})

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per node call: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates

      --json
          Print one JSON object instead of text

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
